[0.000, "o", "ANSWER: The longest file is ./notes/gradient-descent.md. It contains notes on gradient descent, a\r\n        method for training a model by taking small steps that reduce the loss. It covers the steps\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "        (start with random weights, compute the loss on a batch, compute the gradient, move against\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "        it by the learning rate, repeat). It also covers the effects of learning rate that is too\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "        large or too small, common variants (Adam, RMSprop, momentum), mini-batches, normalising\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "        inputs, and overfitting with early stopping or regularisation. The other files are shorter:\r\n        trip.md is a Cox's Bazar trip plan, budget.md is a CSE club budget, and schedule.md is a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "        class timetable. Lengths are estimated from the text I read, not from file metadata.\r\n"]
